melody:
# Chorus as published in 1925 (cut time, written here with quarter-note beats)
Five foot two, eyes of blue,
G4 Bb4 G4 r G4 B4 G4 r/
but oh! what those five foot could do,
G4/ G4 C5 G4 C5 G4 C5 G4
has an-y-bod-y seen my girl?
C5 Eb5 C5 Eb5 C5 Bb4(2) C5(2) G4(4) r(4)
Turned up nose, turned down hose,
G4 Bb4 G4 r G4 B4 G4 r
flap-per, yes sir! One of those,
G4 C5 G4 C5 G4 C5 G4
has an-y-bod-y seen my girl?
C5 Eb5 C5 Eb5 C5 Bb4(2) G4(2) Eb4(4) ~Eb4
Now if you run in-to a five foot two
G4 F#4 G4 D5 Eb5 D5 r/ G4/ D5 Eb5 D5 r
cov-ered with fur,
D5 C5 D5 C5 ~C5(4)
dia-mond rings and all those things,
C5 D5 C5 r/ F4/ C5 D5 C5 r
bet-cha' life it is-n't her!
D5 F5 D5 Bb4 Ab4/ G4 F4/ ~F4
But could she love, could she woo?
F#4 G4 Bb4 G4 r G4 B4 G4 r
Could she, could she, could she coo?
G4 C5 G4 C5 G4 C5 G4
Has an-y-bod-y seen my girl?
C5 Eb5 C5 Eb5 C5 Bb4(2) C5(2) Eb5(4) ~Eb5 r r(2)

